Begin Exploring Related Columns
Below is the reasoning map (tables / columns / possible filters) followed by 10 exploratory‐to‑final SQL statements (each limited to 20 rows and preceded by a short comment).

Relevant tables, columns and why  
• web_orders  
  – id : primary‑key of each order – will be counted.  
  – account_id : joins to web_accounts.id.  
  – total_amt_usd : dollar amount to sum for sales.  
  – occurred_at : can be used for date filters if needed (not required here).  

• web_accounts  
  – id : joins to web_orders.account_id.  
  – sales_rep_id : joins to web_sales_reps.id (who “owns” that account).  
  – name / website etc. – not required for this task.  

• web_sales_reps  
  – id : joins to web_accounts.sales_rep_id.  
  – name : full name of the rep to display.  
  – region_id : joins to web_region.id (to know the rep’s region).  

• web_region  
  – id : joins to web_sales_reps.region_id.  
  – name : region name to group the report by.  

Conditions we may use  
• join keys:  
  web_orders.account_id = web_accounts.id  
  web_accounts.sales_rep_id = web_sales_reps.id  
  web_sales_reps.region_id = web_region.id  
• No additional WHERE filters are requested.

--------------------------------------------------------------------
Exploration & solution‑building SQL (each LIMITED 20 rows)
--------------------------------------------------------------------

```sql
-- 1. Distinct regions available
SELECT DISTINCT r."id", r."name"
FROM "web_region" AS r
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 2. Quick look at some orders (order id, account, sales amount)
SELECT o."id", o."account_id", o."total_amt_usd"
FROM "web_orders" AS o
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 3. Verify mapping between an order and its account / sales rep
SELECT o."id" AS order_id,
       a."name" AS account_name,
       a."sales_rep_id"
FROM "web_orders"  AS o
JOIN "web_accounts" AS a
  ON o."account_id" = a."id"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 4. List some reps and their region
SELECT sr."id"    AS rep_id,
       sr."name"  AS rep_name,
       r."name"   AS region_name
FROM "web_sales_reps" AS sr
JOIN "web_region"     AS r
  ON sr."region_id" = r."id"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 5. Join everything for a few sample rows to be sure the keys work
SELECT o."id"                AS order_id,
       r."name"              AS region,
       sr."name"             AS rep_name,
       o."total_amt_usd"     AS order_amount
FROM   "web_orders"     AS o
JOIN   "web_accounts"   AS a  ON o."account_id" = a."id"
JOIN   "web_sales_reps" AS sr ON a."sales_rep_id" = sr."id"
JOIN   "web_region"     AS r  ON sr."region_id"  = r."id"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 6. Aggregate: number of orders and total sales per region  (sanity check)
SELECT r."name"                        AS region,
       COUNT(o."id")                   AS num_orders,
       SUM(o."total_amt_usd")          AS total_sales
FROM   "web_orders"     AS o
JOIN   "web_accounts"   AS a  ON o."account_id" = a."id"
JOIN   "web_sales_reps" AS sr ON a."sales_rep_id" = sr."id"
JOIN   "web_region"     AS r  ON sr."region_id"  = r."id"
GROUP BY r."name"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 7. Aggregate: total sales per rep inside each region
SELECT r."name"               AS region,
       sr."id"                AS rep_id,
       sr."name"              AS rep_name,
       SUM(o."total_amt_usd") AS rep_sales
FROM   "web_orders"     AS o
JOIN   "web_accounts"   AS a  ON o."account_id" = a."id"
JOIN   "web_sales_reps" AS sr ON a."sales_rep_id" = sr."id"
JOIN   "web_region"     AS r  ON sr."region_id"  = r."id"
GROUP BY r."name", sr."id", sr."name"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 8. For each region, find the single maximum rep_sales value
SELECT region,
       MAX(rep_sales) AS max_rep_sales
FROM (
        SELECT r."name"               AS region,
               sr."id"                AS rep_id,
               SUM(o."total_amt_usd") AS rep_sales
        FROM   "web_orders"     AS o
        JOIN   "web_accounts"   AS a  ON o."account_id" = a."id"
        JOIN   "web_sales_reps" AS sr ON a."sales_rep_id" = sr."id"
        JOIN   "web_region"     AS r  ON sr."region_id"  = r."id"
        GROUP BY r."name", sr."id"
     )
GROUP BY region
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 9. Bring together orders / total sales per region PLUS each rep’s sales;
--    we’ll use it as a CTE for the final answer
WITH rep_sales AS (
     SELECT r."name"               AS region,
            sr."id"                AS rep_id,
            sr."name"              AS rep_name,
            SUM(o."total_amt_usd") AS rep_sales
     FROM   "web_orders"     AS o
     JOIN   "web_accounts"   AS a  ON o."account_id" = a."id"
     JOIN   "web_sales_reps" AS sr ON a."sales_rep_id" = sr."id"
     JOIN   "web_region"     AS r  ON sr."region_id"  = r."id"
     GROUP BY r."name", sr."id", sr."name"
)
SELECT *
FROM rep_sales
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 10. FINAL ANSWER: full web‑sales report per region
WITH
-- A. total orders / sales per region
region_totals AS (
    SELECT r."name"               AS region,
           COUNT(o."id")          AS num_orders,
           SUM(o."total_amt_usd") AS total_sales
    FROM   "web_orders"     AS o
    JOIN   "web_accounts"   AS a  ON o."account_id" = a."id"
    JOIN   "web_sales_reps" AS sr ON a."sales_rep_id" = sr."id"
    JOIN   "web_region"     AS r  ON sr."region_id"  = r."id"
    GROUP BY r."name"
),
-- B. sales per rep per region
rep_sales AS (
    SELECT r."name"               AS region,
           sr."name"              AS rep_name,
           SUM(o."total_amt_usd") AS rep_sales
    FROM   "web_orders"     AS o
    JOIN   "web_accounts"   AS a  ON o."account_id" = a."id"
    JOIN   "web_sales_reps" AS sr ON a."sales_rep_id" = sr."id"
    JOIN   "web_region"     AS r  ON sr."region_id"  = r."id"
    GROUP BY r."name", sr."name"
),
-- C. find the maximum rep_sales value within each region
max_rep_sales AS (
    SELECT region,
           MAX(rep_sales) AS max_sales_in_region
    FROM   rep_sales
    GROUP BY region
)
-- D. assemble the report, keeping all reps who tie for the max
SELECT rt.region,
       rt.num_orders,
       rt.total_sales,
       rs.rep_name,
       rs.rep_sales AS top_rep_sales
FROM   region_totals   AS rt
JOIN   max_rep_sales   AS mx ON rt.region = mx.region
JOIN   rep_sales       AS rs ON rs.region = mx.region
                               AND rs.rep_sales = mx.max_sales_in_region
ORDER  BY rt.region
LIMIT 20;
```

Each query is unique, uses only provided tables, and gradually builds toward the requested detailed web‑sales report, listing every sales representative who ties for the highest total sales amount in his/her region.
